fact WorkItem(id: "WI-287", description: some(value: "Typer: match expression takes branch-0 type, ignores other branches (no lub/join) — soundness gap. MatchFinal (rustland/anthill-core/src/kb/typing.rs:~1362) sets the match result type to the FIRST branch's type and never joins or cross-checks the remaining branches. There is no lub/join over branch types anywhere in the typer. Consequence (unsound): a match whose branches have incompatible types is accepted. Two leaks, both demonstrated by failing tests: (1) synthesis mode — `let x = match t { case on -> 1; case off -> \"hello\" }` types x as Int (branch 0); the String branch is checked against expected=None, i.e. nothing. (2) declared-return mode — `operation pick(t) -> Int = match t { case on -> 1; case off -> \"hello\" }` ALSO loads clean: body_expected reaches branches as an inference HINT, not an enforced check, and the op-body return check only inspects the synthesized match type (branch 0 = Int). Anchor: a direct `-> Int` op body of \"hello\" IS rejected, proving return-type checking works in general and the leak is specifically the match first-branch-wins shortcut. Tests: rustland/anthill-core/tests/include/match_branch_join_test.rs (wired into wi_tests). The two branch-clash tests assert the SOUND behavior so they fail on the bug; currently #[ignore]d to keep the suite green — run with --ignored to see them fail; remove #[ignore] when fixed (they become regression guards). Fix direction: compute a join (lub) over branch types in MatchFinal, using the Type lattice (Lattice[T=Type], glb/lub) + entity-instance widening (constructor_parent_sort climbs entity -> enclosing sort). Top-less lattice: incompatible branches with no common supertype (Int vs String) must be a type error, not silently accepted. Decide whether match is checked (every branch <: expected when an expected type is present) AND/OR synthesized (join when not). Related design discussion: widen / entity-singleton (Type.singleton(ExprOccurrence) is reserved-but-unused; check_bare_ref at typing.rs:949 collapses leaf precision eagerly to a nameable sort / anthill.prelude.Type), docs/proposals/011-type-resolution.md. Note: scaland has a parallel typer that should get the same fix + tests to avoid divergence."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-05-23T14:26:13Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-287", author: "user", content: "Delivered (commit pending). ROOT CAUSE: MatchFinal set the match type to branch 0 (result_ty = Some(body_r.ty), first-branch-wins); IfExpr returned then_r.ty and its frame didn't even carry expected. Leaves (literals/refs) ignore expected, so it was an inference HINT, never enforced; the only enforcement was the op-body return check, which saw the synthesized type = branch 0. Hence Int/String branch clashes loaded clean in both synthesis (let x = match) and declared-return (op body) positions.\n\nFIX (rustland/anthill-core/src/kb/typing.rs): new compute_branch_join_type(kb, branch_tys, expected, construct) — checked mode (expected present): every branch must types_compatible with it (covers entity->sort + requires-refine); synthesis mode: fold branch types with join_types. Threaded body_expected into MatchFinal and expected into IfExpr frames; both call the shared helper. join_types = commutative common-supertype: type_var short-circuit, directional types_compatible (supertype wins), more_general_type for the mutually-compatible (bare-vs-parameterized) case, else entity->enclosing-sort widening climb (bounded 0..64), else None.\n\nSCOPE: ALSO fixed if (identical first-branch-wins gap; user asked) via the same helper — extends past the WI's match-only text.\n\nDESIGN (sound common supertype, NOT strict lub): the synthesized result is an upper bound, not the lattice-theoretic lub. For bare-vs-parameterized (none():Option vs some(1):Option[T=Int], mutually types_compatible) the STRICT lub is Option[T=Int] (none is polymorphic), but the typer neither tracks that a bare type is the polymorphic kind nor unifies at the join, so more_general_type returns the conservative bare Option (user-confirmed choice) — never over-claims a binding a declared -> Option might not have. Checked mode prefers the precise join but never widens past expected and never collapses to a type_var hint (would lose the concrete type for a match/if passed as a generic arg).\n\nTESTS (wi_tests, 7 total, all green): un-ignored the 2 match clash tests + anchor (match_branch_join_test.rs); new if_branch_join_test.rs = synthesis clash, op-body clash, positive control (if c then 1 else 2 loads clean), bare/param join in both branch orders.\n\nCODE-REVIEW (max, 5 angles + sweep): (1) FIXED — join_types was order-dependent for bare-vs-param (types_compatible true both ways); made commutative via more_general_type. (2) FIXED — (clash, Some(exp)) arm could collapse a genuine clash to a wildcard if exp were a type_var; added type_var guard (currently unreachable — args use push_visit_no_hint, op/let/lambda hints are concrete — but self-consistent). LEFT (documented, not bugs): 0..64 climb bound (defensive, single-level entity->sort today, unbounded would be worse); exhaustiveness diagnostic skipped when a branch ALSO has a type error (type error is the more fundamental signal); min_sort now more-defined for a branch with an unresolved arm (suite confirms no [simp] regression).\n\nSCALAND: WI text said 'scaland has a parallel typer that should get the same fix' — INACCURATE. scaland has NO expression typer yet (user-confirmed; zero subtype/lub/types_compatible machinery). Nothing to port; recorded so future 'mirror in scaland' typer notes don't mislead.\n\nVALIDATION: full anthill-core suite 0 failures (incl. all 7 branch tests, 218 lib, wi_tests, eval/github_todo/algebra/builtin/induction/resolve).", at: "2026-05-23T14:26:39Z")
